<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine monthly grain/oilseed shipments.</title>
<headline>Argentine monthly grain/oilseed shipments.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agriculture Secretariat March grain shipment figures (tonnes), followed by January-March totals (year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> Wheat	822,349  (493,132)     5,046,102  (1,812,473)</p>
<p> Maize    1,235,212  (545,462)     1,681,684    (715,255)</p>
<p> Sorghum     81,312    32,072	   81,312     (32,072)</p>
<p> Barley	68,414     (nil)	  140,349	(6,888)</p>
<p> Soybeans	 nil    87,784		968    (102,296)</p>
<p> Sunseed	  821  (350,258)	   1,690    (394,242)</p>
<p> Others	13,203   (22,267)	  62,611     (40,613)</p>
<p>Principal destinations in March were as follows (tonnes):  </p>
<p>WHEAT: Brazil 444,439; Egypt 71,541; Peru 62,349; South Korea 35,570; Nigeria 28,688; Turkey 27,198</p>
<p>MAIZE: Egypt 155,130; South Africa 129,360; Morocco 118,278; South Korea 85,980; Tunisia 61,170; Turkey 60,776</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
